	abstract = {Abstract: The recent era, RFID-tags enabled hallmark transparency potential attributes are addition the value in Jewellery Supply Chain Responsiveness (JSCR). Therefore, there is a key necessity to real-time transparency \& traceability potential attributes encompasses from upstream \& downstream in SC stakeholders. The addition of value in jewellery SC business, which pertains to jewellery inventory accuracy, transparency of shop-floor activities, visibility in multi-tiers JSC stakeholders and hallmarks visibility for Efficient Customer Responsiveness (ECR). The objectives of this research paper is to identify the RFID-enabled hallmark transparency potential attributes inter-relationship and ranking preference orders of performance criterion among the JSCR. The proposed framework is consists of 10 transparency and traceability attributes linkages and dependent relationships jewellery business organizations. The case study is focused on Indian Tanishq Jewellery manufacturing and marketing business 4P strategies implementations namely Product innovation strategy, Price strategy, Place strategy, Promotion Planning strategy. The addition of value through trust to hallmarks transparency jewellery visibilities (transparency, traceability and trust alignments) are enhanced the trust in multi-tags ownership transactions among the multiple -SC stakeholders and end customer responsible to ECR. ISM approach is used to model inter-relationships among transparency potential attributes responsible in JSCR. MICMAC analysis provides the precise analysis relationship among the driving and dependence powers linkages ability in JSCM. AHP approach is implemented for identify the weight priority of RFID enables transparency performance criterion in Jewellery SC responsiveness. The ranking sequence orders of jewellery transparency performance criterion weights are first Cost-Effectiveness (CE) {\textgreater} Break-even tag price decision (BETPD) {\textgreater} Effective lead time reduction (ELTR) {\textgreater} Efficient Customer Response (ECR) {\textgreater}SC visibility, trust \& traceability (SCV\&T). RFID tags enable technology can be more responsive to trust and transparency addition of jewellery organizations. Jewellery managers can be benefits by overcomes of financial losses such as reduction of operational handling cost, misplacement errors reduction and inventory inaccuracy problems etc. Keywords: Supply chain responsiveness, Jewellery SC, ISM, RFID-tags, E-Retail, and ECR.},
	language = {en},
	journal = {International Journal of Process Management and Benchmarking},
	author = {Kumar, Mukesh},
	month = jun,
	year = {2023},
	file = {Kumar - 2023 - Modelling of RFID-enables jewellery hallmark trans:/Users/corywhitney/Zotero/storage/WWFDW3P8/Kumar - 2023 - Modelling of RFID-enables jewellery hallmark trans.pdf:application/pdf},
