“It is well known, however, that this estimator-first approach is remarkably easy to go awry when the relations between state variables are less understood. For instance, Judea Pearl commenting on popularity of regression models noted that the lack of explicit problem structure may easily fool researchers to control for causes or mediators instead of confounders, with predictably bad results [12].”
“Influence diagrams are a primary method of visualizing relations between parts of the decision problem but are, strictly speaking, not required for modeling because all the information needed for evaluation and appraisal can be captured in the join”
