	abstract = {The current Air Traffic Management functional approach is changing: ‘time’ is now integrated as an additional fourth dimension on trajectories. This concept will impose on aircraft the compliance of accurately arrival times over designated checkpoints, called Time Windows (TWs). We characterise these TWs with a stochastic approach (Monte Carlo simulations), and manage the uncertainty associated to the evolution of 4D-trajectories with a causal and predictability analysis, using a Bayesian Networks methodology. Then, we analyse the 4D-trajectory reliability through Multi State Systems and Markov Chains models, which may allow stakeholders to establish performance indicators and compliance metrics.},
