@book{henson_healthcare_2023,
	series = {Healthcare {Financial} {Management}: {Applied} {Concepts} and {Practical} {Analyses}},
	title = {Healthcare financial management: applied concepts and practical analyses},
	shorttitle = {Healthcare financial management},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85166100982&doi=10.1891%2f9780826144751&partnerID=40&md5=81d90e9c6b00073f0fc3dfd38dabfff7},
	language = {en},
	author = {Henson, C.},
	year = {2023},
	doi = {10.1891/9780826144751},
	note = {Pages: 342},
	annote = {Abstract
Healthcare financial management and the business processes that surround it have become a more common fixture in the academic space. Historically, the challenge has been communicating how healthcare finance impacts other functional areas within the typical healthcare organization. This textbook addresses this challenge. The discipline of healthcare finance is business-adjacent, and while all aspects of business operations are important, the patient and the financial functions that surround them in the healthcare arena affect every part of the organization. How do you teach healthcare professionals, specifically those without finance backgrounds, to recognize this? How do you keep students engaged and interested in learning more about the discipline? What do you teach them to ensure that the learned concepts are relevant, no matter the setting? Preparing the next generation of healthcare management and administration professionals is no easy feat, given the breadth of knowledge required to operate effectively and efficiently. The subject needs to be approachable, accessible, and user-friendly in order to educate students and healthcare professionals from all backgrounds. The book, which is composed of five modules, meets students where there are, and then brings them along to where we need them to be. The book discusses the basics of accounting and finance as the backdrop to the much broader scope of healthcare financial management. Finance is more than just the annual budget process; everything we do in healthcare has a financial impact. The textbook material is then applied to a course project by having students prepare various financial calculations as they would be prepared by a healthcare organization’s finance department. The textbook’s applied approach presents a learning curve for students unfamiliar with healthcare finance or spreadsheets, and the hands-on work performed will help them develop a valuable knowledge base in different kinds of data analyses and organizational decision-making.
},
	annote = {Export Date: 05 May 2024; Cited By: 0},
}

