	annote = {nterdependent-decision analysis is an important research stream in the area of decision sciences in recent years. Particularly, the development of studies on interdependent-decision analysis with crossorganizations, cross-processes, cross-tasks and cross-stages is promoted by supply chain integration and the management of collaboration innovation. Systematic review on the newest trends in this area will contribute to clear the research streams, improve the effectiveness of method application and promote state-of-the-art research development. Firstly, an in-depth analysis of interdependent-decision elements is conducted to clarify the changes of research trends as well as the differences and features of different decision elements in terms of types, structures and information. Then, interdependent-decision analysis methods in the existing literature are classified according to the applicative scenarios. Furthermore, to know the applicable and theoretical values, these methods are compared from the perspectives of principles, innovation and contribution, information processing capabilities and application complexities. Finally, new research opportunities of interdependent-decision analysis methods are discussed.
